<!--
  Status-bar icon: the Penrose mark as a flat silhouette.

  Android tints small notification icons to a single colour and uses only their
  alpha, so anything with opaque colour in it collapses into a filled blob. The
  launcher icon has the same constraint and solves it with a luminance-to-alpha
  monochrome layer, but that trick needs more pixels than 24dp gives, and the
  three cube-face shades that carry the impossible-triangle illusion are not
  separable at this size anyway. A clean silhouette of the tribar is the honest
  treatment here and still reads as the mark.

  Geometry generated from src-tauri/images/logo.svg: nine isometric cubes, each
  the hexagonal outline of its three faces, centres straight out of the source
  art with its translate(10,0) applied. Regenerate from that file rather than
  hand-editing these numbers if the mark ever changes.

  Drawn as one path with nine subpaths, all wound the same way, so nonZero fill
  unions the overlaps into a single shape instead of punching holes where the
  cubes touch.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="124"
    android:viewportHeight="124">
